1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:17,400
A Place of Our Own

2
00:00:17,400 --> 00:00:21,000
I remember your parents' first house very well.

3
00:00:21,000 --> 00:00:23,900
It was on Spring Avenue, near the park.

4
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:24,900
I grew up in that house.

5
00:00:24,900 --> 00:00:27,100
Yes, and you were such a cute baby.

6
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:29,039
I've seen pictures of him.

7
00:00:29,039 --> 00:00:31,100
He had blond hair.

8
00:00:31,100 --> 00:00:32,000
I've been friendly with the Stewart family

9
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:33,200
for a long time,

10
00:00:33,200 --> 00:00:34,100
so it's my pleasure

11
00:00:34,100 --> 00:00:35,500
to help you find a house now.

12
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:37,800
Well, we're not sure we can afford one.

13
00:00:37,800 --> 00:00:39,100
But we'd like to find out

14
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:39,800
about the possibilities.

15
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:41,500
That's a good idea.

16
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:44,300
I love your house on Linden Street.

17
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:46,700
I sold your father that house seventeen years ago.

18
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,000
Really?

19
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,500
Yes, Mom was pregnant with Robbie then,

20
00:00:49,500 --> 00:00:51,600
and they needed the extra room.

21
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:53,000
I hear you're expecting a baby, Mrs. Stewart.

22
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:53,900
Mmm-hmm.

23
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:56,000
So we will be needing more room.

24
00:00:56,000 --> 00:00:57,500
Oh, so you don't need something immediately?

25
00:00:57,500 --> 00:00:59,400
No. But in five or six months ...

26
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,500
And time passes so quickly.

27
00:01:01,500 --> 00:01:03,700
Yes, it does.

28
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:04,300
Well, when you called,

29
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:05,700
you gave me enough information

30
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:07,900
about your salaries and your savings.

31
00:01:07,900 --> 00:01:10,700
So I have a good idea about your financial situation.

32
00:01:10,700 --> 00:01:13,100
Let me show you some pictures of houses.

33
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:14,460
With two bedrooms?

34
00:01:14,460 --> 00:01:16,000
Yes, I think I can show you some.

35
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:18,500
Of course, they won't be in Riverdale.

36
00:01:18,500 --> 00:01:21,700
The cost of housing's too high for you here.

37
00:01:21,700 --> 00:01:24,400
I haven't thought about living anywhere else.

38
00:01:24,400 --> 00:01:26,800
We've always lived in this area.

39
00:01:26,800 --> 00:01:28,832
Where should we look for a house, Mrs. Martinelli?

40
00:01:28,832 --> 00:01:30,637
Well, we have an office in Mount Kisco.

41
00:01:30,637 --> 00:01:31,737
It's a lovely area,

42
00:01:31,737 --> 00:01:34,021
and it's only about an hour's drive from here.

43
00:01:34,021 --> 00:01:35,200
Here.

44
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:39,600
I have a book with photos of some homes in that area.

45
00:01:39,600 --> 00:01:44,300
Now, let's see. Here.

46
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:48,929
This is a lovely two-bedroom house in your price range.

47
00:01:48,929 --> 00:01:52,000
It's pretty,

48
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:53,700
but I prefer a two-story home.

49
00:01:53,700 --> 00:01:55,000
I do, too.

50
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
I don't care for a ranch type.

51
00:01:57,000 --> 00:02:00,300
OK.

52
00:02:00,300 --> 00:02:02,700
Oh, this is a wonderful house.

53
00:02:02,700 --> 00:02:03,800
I know it well.

54
00:02:03,800 --> 00:02:05,000
I sold it to the present owners.

55
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:06,620
It looks wonderful.

56
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,400
This is a two-bedroom, two-bath house.

57
00:02:08,400 --> 00:02:10,400
It has a full basement,

58
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:12,600
and it is on a half-acre lot.

59
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:14,900
You can probably afford this one.

60
00:02:14,900 --> 00:02:16,100
I like this house.

61
00:02:16,100 --> 00:02:16,800
So do I.

62
00:02:16,800 --> 00:02:19,200
And the price is right.

63
00:02:19,200 --> 00:02:19,900
Would you like to go see it?

64
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:20,500
Yes. We're planning

65
00:02:20,500 --> 00:02:23,200
to talk to someone at the bank next week.

66
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:25,000
Perhaps we could see the house this weekend.

67
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:26,700
If someone doesn't buy it before then,

68
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:30,806
But let's keep looking.

69
00:02:30,806 --> 00:02:33,000
Just to get an idea of some other possibilities.

70
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:37,100
This is very helpful, Mrs. Martinelli.

71
00:02:37,100 --> 00:02:37,950
Here.

72
00:02:37,950 --> 00:02:41,400
This is a wonderful example of Spanish-style architecture.

73
00:02:41,400 --> 00:02:42,077
Oh,

74
00:02:42,077 --> 00:02:44,800
I love the roof tiles on a Spanish-style house.

75
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:48,074
It looks like the houses in Hollywood.

76
00:02:48,074 --> 00:02:49,259
It's interesting.

77
00:02:49,259 --> 00:03:01,100
A house like this in Riverdale costs double the price.

78
00:03:01,100 --> 00:03:04,100
Oh my!

79
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,400
Here's a real buy.

80
00:03:06,400 --> 00:03:07,600
It's a bargain.

81
00:03:07,600 --> 00:03:10,200
This house just came on the market.

82
00:03:10,200 --> 00:03:11,100
It's quite lovely.

83
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:12,400
Is it a two-bedroom house?

84
00:03:12,400 --> 00:03:15,100
No. It has three bedrooms and three baths.

85
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,600
I know the house.

86
00:03:16,600 --> 00:03:18,200
It has a brand new kitchen.

87
00:03:18,200 --> 00:03:21,000
And a living room with a twelve-foot ceiling.

88
00:03:21,000 --> 00:03:22,976
And there's a two-car garage.

89
00:03:22,976 --> 00:03:24,659
Then why don't we go look at this house, too?

90
00:03:24,659 --> 00:03:26,800
It's a good investment.

91
00:03:26,800 --> 00:03:27,921
Thank you, Mrs. Martinelli.

92
00:03:27,921 --> 00:03:28,600
Thanks so much.

93
00:03:28,600 --> 00:03:30,600
My pleasure.

94
00:03:30,600 --> 00:03:32,433
Give my best to your parents.

95
00:03:32,433 --> 00:03:34,800
Your father's a wonderful doctor, Richard.

96
00:03:34,800 --> 00:03:37,000
He took care of my daughter

97
00:03:37,000 --> 00:03:39,300
when she was a child.

98
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:39,500
He's the best pediatrician in Westchester.

99
00:03:39,300 --> 00:03:40,600
Thanks, Mrs. Martinelli.

100
00:03:40,600 --> 00:03:41,000
I'll give them your regards.

101
00:03:41,000 --> 00:03:44,200
We really appreciate your advice.

102
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,600
I do think you should go see the houses

103
00:03:45,600 --> 00:03:46,900
and talk to the bank.

104
00:03:46,900 --> 00:03:47,500
Here.

105
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:55,000
Let me give you some information sheets about the houses.

106
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:57,600
They're both very good buys.

107
00:03:57,600 --> 00:03:59,100
Well, thanks so much for your help and your time,

108
00:03:59,100 --> 00:04:01,300
Mrs. Martinelli.

109
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:02,200
We've got a lot to talk about.

110
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:05,200
Mmm-hmm. Thanks.
